1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:02,876
MyCampusView Academy.

2
00:00:02,926 --> 00:00:05,201
Tiny Coders, video 1.

3
00:00:05,251 --> 00:00:09,520
Welcome: you already give instructions.

4
00:00:10,650 --> 00:00:14,721
Welcome to Tiny Coders from MyCampusView Academy!

5
00:00:14,771 --> 00:00:18,001
Coding means giving clear instructions.

6
00:00:18,051 --> 00:00:22,710
You already do this when you explain a game or a recipe.

7
00:00:24,050 --> 00:00:28,728
Coding means writing instructions a computer can follow.

8
00:00:28,778 --> 00:00:31,852
Computers are careful but not clever.

9
00:00:31,902 --> 00:00:36,580
They only do exactly what you ask, in the order you ask.

10
00:00:37,950 --> 00:00:39,925
Three classroom rules.

11
00:00:39,975 --> 00:00:43,514
Be kind when someone’s plan goes wrong.

12
00:00:43,564 --> 00:00:47,471
Try again after a mistake — that is normal.

13
00:00:47,521 --> 00:00:51,060
Ask for help after you have tried once.

14
00:00:52,450 --> 00:00:55,645
Remember: coding is ordered steps.

15
00:00:55,695 --> 00:00:56,981
Order matters.

16
00:00:57,031 --> 00:01:00,990
And bugs are normal — they help you learn.

17
00:01:02,500 --> 00:01:03,869
Let us recap.

18
00:01:03,919 --> 00:01:08,453
Coding is clear step-by-step instructions.

19
00:01:08,503 --> 00:01:09,981
Order matters.

20
00:01:10,031 --> 00:01:12,927
Mistakes are how you learn.

21
00:01:12,977 --> 00:01:15,110
Next: Order matters.
